  {
   "caption": "Read as 2's complement, the order breaks between 011 (+3) and 100 (−4): the bigger field holds the smaller exponent. A float with exponent −1 (111) would compare above one with exponent +3 (011).",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "tab",
